A||||7||Shiner||Noisy Interior||||8||
Z||000000||Shiner||11-07-2001||02:55 PM||||The interior of my GT is really creaking pretty good over even somewhat rough roads.  I plan on pulling most of it and replacing it with another interior I have (painting it black).  What can I do to cut down on some of this noise?  It drives me about crazy sometimes!<P>TTA!<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||8
Z||000001||OcalaFiero||11-07-2001||03:11 PM||||Alot of the creaks that I had in mine went away when I replaced the door hinge bushings and adjusted the lock striker. The doors seem to be big culprits here. Also check the plastic trim over the door and the "A" pillar.<P><P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>Ocala, Florida<BR>'86 2M4<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallsigpic_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTBro||11-07-2001||03:12 PM||||Go to your local auto sound retailer and ask them for a product called Dynamat.  I think it is quite pricey, but it will do the job.  It is specially formulated to decrease unwanted road noise and vibration.  It comes in sheets.  You just cut to size, peel the backing and stick it anywhere you like.  Preferably on the floor, under door panels, firewall, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||11-07-2001||03:51 PM||||I have this annyoing squeak whenever my car is moving... I believe it's my quarter window.  I had just replaced them this summer with the reproduction ones and now that's it's cold outside I've been hearing that squeak.<P>Another place all of my squeaks come from are the seats.  Used to have the sunroof squeak, but that seems to be better now.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jaei Sun||11-07-2001||04:08 PM||||Congrats you own a GM!<P>I have the same problem but this winter I'm doing some major work to the interior.<P>1st I'm removing every panel and putting the really spendy version of Dynomat in (the silver reflective stuff) all over the sheet metal.<P>2nd On the other side of the trim, I will be fiberglassing the whole back side with 2 layers of glass.<P>3rd When assembling back together will be using all new "christmas trees".<P>Hopefully it will get rid of 95% of the unwanted noises that plague my fiero.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/Jaei_blue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||11-07-2001||08:22 PM||||I just bought a loud stereo instead  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero2.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
